WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.360
Devon now commits 89% of cognition's own code as the lab hits a $1 billion run rate. That figure sits on a $48 billion valuation. This is Models &amp; Agents Episode 209. After cognition, we get X's search API, Inception's diffusion model, the agent governance problem, and the local boxes people are actually wiring up, then things to try on the horizon and an engineering tear down.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:34.540
Cognition AI Magazine reports posted the jump on September 25th, 2026, up from $492 million

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:41.440
in May after raising more than $2 billion. Devon plans, writes, tests, and commits, and a

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.240
human reviews what it produced. Scott Wu, the chief executive, says the agent currently lands

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:53.100
between a junior and a mid-level engineer. Goldman Sachs, Mercedes-Benz, GE Aerospace,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.680
base and new bank are on the customer list, with distribution deals at Infosys, Cognizant

00:00:58.680 --> 00:00:59.480
and AWS.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:05.980
Mercedes-Benz put more than 200,000 lines of cobalt through Devon, and new banks saw 8-12

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.500
times efficiency gains on large migrations.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:15.240
Cognition bought windsurf in July 2025, and gained an agentic integrated development environment

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.340
or IDE that sits beside Devon in a working developer's day.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:25.690
Exha shipped Exha 3.0 as an upgrade to its web search API for AI agents,

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.910
MarkTech Post reports, with a larger embedding model and a cheaper light search type

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:33.350
priced at $4 per 1000 requests.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:38.150
Dynamic highlights is now generally available and it picks tokens across

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.130
results instead of page by page.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:46.610
That path uses 95% fewer tokens than full page text and still improves answer quality.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:52.030
Exha says the new version leads perplexity, brave, and parallel on all eight of its

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:59.550
self-run benchmarks, with the widest gaps on Browse Comp at 91.8%, and Atlas at 42%.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:04.670
The company runs its own crawler and an independent index covering more than two trillion URLs,

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:06.990
and there is no self-hosted option.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:13.230
Light accepts query, result count, highlights, text, categories, domain and date filters,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.170
plus location and moderation.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:21.739
Mercury 3, a diffusion language model from Inception, fills in many tokens at once instead

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:24.459
of one after another, Mark Tech Post reports.

00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:31.999
It hits 1068 tokens per second on NVIDIA GPUs and carries a 1 million token context window.

00:02:32.539 --> 00:02:39.599
On Inception's own table, Mercury 3 leads GPT-6 Luna and Claude Haiku 5.5 on 8 of 12 tests

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:44.559
at medium settings, with its biggest gains on instruction following and agentic coding.

00:02:44.559 --> 00:02:50.519
The model is more than 40 times larger than Mercury 1, an average quality across standard

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:56.039
benchmarks rose roughly three times across those generations while speed-state above 1000 tokens

00:02:56.039 --> 00:03:02.499
per second. Serving is only through Inceptions and Vidya GPU API, with no open weights and

00:03:02.499 --> 00:03:11.951
no quantized builds. The author of Cynthia put out Tess 4.5-27b, a Quinn 3.8-27b fine-tune,

00:03:11.951 --> 00:03:14.311
in the local Lama community on Reddit.

00:03:14.791 --> 00:03:16.651
It matches the same benchmark scores

00:03:16.651 --> 00:03:19.051
with 25% fewer tokens overall.

00:03:19.611 --> 00:03:22.991
On the hardest subsets, CLI-40 and data extraction,

00:03:23.571 --> 00:03:26.311
the cut is 32% to 43% fewer tokens.

00:03:27.251 --> 00:03:29.391
GGUF weights are up on hugging face.

00:03:30.031 --> 00:03:32.171
Burning fewer tokens means faster answers

00:03:32.171 --> 00:03:34.971
and longer sessions before the context window fills.

00:03:35.571 --> 00:03:37.511
And that stacks with draft head acceleration

00:03:37.511 --> 00:03:39.211
on local GPUs.

00:03:39.211 --> 00:03:44.998
Enterprises now have to track and secure their own proliferating AI agents, not only

00:03:44.998 --> 00:03:47.778
fend off external rogue ones, CIO reports.

00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:51.118
Most organizations still lack basic visibility.

00:03:51.678 --> 00:03:58.038
Anthropics says 82% have found unregistered agents on their networks, and 57% already run

00:03:58.038 --> 00:03:59.818
agents on multi-stage workflows.

00:04:00.338 --> 00:04:06.418
Standing up an agent is one API call, or vibe coding by any employee, so vendor, platform

00:04:06.418 --> 00:04:11.698
native and homegrown agents pile onto the sprawl. Security teams need a single record

00:04:11.698 --> 00:04:17.278
per agent that captures onboarding owner, access privileges, behavior, and cross-platform

00:04:17.278 --> 00:04:22.738
capabilities. An over-provisioned email agent with 50 attached tools is the example worth

00:04:22.738 --> 00:04:29.614
investigating. Switch, from Sandbox AQ, now watches AI agents spend, performance metrics

00:04:29.614 --> 00:04:36.174
and security posture in one view, HPC Wire reports. Security and finance teams get unified

00:04:36.174 --> 00:04:42.354
telemetry across every platform an agent runs on. Cybersecurity experts told Think Digital Partners

00:04:42.354 --> 00:04:47.954
that autonomous agents need new digital identity frameworks because human-centric controls break

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:54.429
down when agents act on their own across systems. A builder on Reddit's local Alma Forum plans to

00:04:54.429 --> 00:05:04.569
buy a used HP Z640 with dual E52680 V4 CPUs and 64 gigabytes of ECC RAM for 550 euros,

00:05:04.569 --> 00:05:11.649
then drop in two RTX 3060 12 gigabyte cards. The intended mix is QN 3.8 flash

00:05:11.649 --> 00:05:17.669
next on strata plus llama.cpp, PyTorch computer vision training, reinforcement

00:05:17.669 --> 00:05:23.689
learning in Pi Bullet, Lora fine tuning and Mini Max H3 video generation. Open

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:28.989
questions are dual socket PCIe layout, power limit adapters for the 3060s,

00:05:28.989 --> 00:05:36.069
Whether the included Quadro M6000 24GB card still helps under Cuda 12 and chassis thermals

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:38.689
that hit 86 degrees Celsius during MemTest.

00:05:39.578 --> 00:05:44.658
Model Fit is a real-time Mac configurator, posted to that same local Alma community

00:05:44.918 --> 00:05:49.538
that shows which large language models fit in memory and what inference speed to expect

00:05:49.538 --> 00:05:51.718
on every Apple Silicon configuration.

00:05:52.338 --> 00:05:57.638
The estimates come from a model fitted on actual Lama Bench runs, Apple list prices refreshed

00:05:57.638 --> 00:06:03.178
daily, and the tool is built to help a buyer pick among M4, M5 Pro, and other

00:06:03.178 --> 00:06:08.102
skews for local work. Low latency streaming speech-to-speech is what voice

00:06:08.102 --> 00:06:13.522
manager ships. Over a single web socket, with barge-in, session memory, and tool-call

00:06:13.522 --> 00:06:18.582
integration, according to a local Alma post. Hermes' console is a Kotlin

00:06:18.582 --> 00:06:23.622
reference client styled after Star Trek L-Cars. The stack uses Nemotron and

00:06:23.622 --> 00:06:29.382
Breeze TTS 2, and it is out under MIT with client integration docs and a Python client.

00:06:30.339 --> 00:06:38.199
Someone running Gemma 431bq5KM at about 2.3 tokens per second on a single RTX 306012

00:06:38.199 --> 00:06:42.839
gigabyte card, wants 15 plus tokens per second at 16,000 context.

00:06:43.259 --> 00:06:49.819
The options on the table in that local Alma thread are an RTX 5060TI 16 gigabyte card

00:06:49.819 --> 00:06:58.359
on a PCIe 3.0X1 riser plus layer splitting, or a cheap dual Tesla Pone 179 or X99 build.

00:06:59.327 --> 00:07:04.287
A Centalian AI agent also today cut trade finance amendment time by 80 percent.

00:07:05.087 --> 00:07:06.287
PYMNTS reports.

00:07:07.087 --> 00:07:11.527
Cognizant and Google Cloud expanded a partnership to scale enterprise AI agents,

00:07:11.947 --> 00:07:13.507
according to HPCWire.

00:07:13.967 --> 00:07:18.327
A security firm found a China-linked AI agent behind Japan Cyberattacks,

00:07:18.327 --> 00:07:23.847
the Straits Times reports. AI agents are changing the manager's job while accountability has

00:07:23.847 --> 00:07:30.187
not caught up. IT brief Australia reports. A new AI model detects hidden diseases in routine

00:07:30.187 --> 00:07:36.607
computed tomography or CT scans, according to News I Am Medical. Documents reveal a military

00:07:36.607 --> 00:07:42.907
plan for agentic AI that hacks United States adversaries, Gizmodo reports. Point your agents

00:07:42.907 --> 00:07:48.287
at XA 3.0 light when you want dynamic highlights instead of swallowing full-page text.

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:54.327
Open model fit before you buy a Mac for local inference, and compare the Lama Bench-derived speed

00:07:54.327 --> 00:08:00.847
estimates across M4 and M5 Pro SKUs. Run Mercury 3 against your current auto-regressive model

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:06.807
on instruction following or agent coding tasks, and feel the parallel decode. Why are voice

00:08:06.807 --> 00:08:12.127
manager to the Hermes console Kotlin client if you need barge in speech-to-speech for a local agent?

00:08:12.127 --> 00:08:16.584
Open AI continues expanding low resource language support,

00:08:16.844 --> 00:08:21.204
co-ball, foretran, visual basic for legacy modernization customers.

00:08:21.664 --> 00:08:26.164
VALTER is rolling out further agentic AI infrastructure upgrades on its platform.

00:08:27.282 --> 00:08:29.942
Web pages wrap the useful bits inside navigation,

00:08:30.582 --> 00:08:33.302
scripts and ads that agents then strip at token cost,

00:08:33.742 --> 00:08:36.602
so let me pop the hood on llms.txt.

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:39.622
The curated markdown file meant to skip that parse.

00:08:39.622 --> 00:08:44.722
The proposal puts one file at the site route that gathers expert-level summaries and links

00:08:44.722 --> 00:08:48.442
to key pages, and that file is the map and agent reads first.

00:08:48.942 --> 00:08:54.042
Context windows are still finite, so every token spent chewing chrome is a token that never

00:08:54.042 --> 00:08:54.962
reaches the answer.

00:08:55.522 --> 00:09:00.482
A clean markdown map lets the agent judge relevance before it fetches full pages, which

00:09:00.482 --> 00:09:03.562
is the step that used to dump a whole human layout into the prompt.

00:09:03.562 --> 00:09:09.062
The V2 revision added standard link relations so the agent does not have to guess the URL.

00:09:09.562 --> 00:09:16.162
Those relations are real alternate with type-text-slash-markdown, and real described by OpenAI,

00:09:16.642 --> 00:09:21.062
Anthropic and Gemini already published their developer docs this way, and documentation

00:09:21.062 --> 00:09:23.562
platforms generate the file automatically.

00:09:24.122 --> 00:09:27.822
The engineering trade-off is maintenance overhead versus retrieval quality.

00:09:28.382 --> 00:09:33.042
Sites that keep the file current see agents land on the right information faster, and

00:09:33.042 --> 00:09:36.362
And a stale file is just another outdated asset sitting at the root.

00:09:36.882 --> 00:09:42.102
Publish one when you already maintain high-quality markdown documentation, and you want coding

00:09:42.102 --> 00:09:44.882
agents or retrieval systems to consume it reliably.

00:09:45.562 --> 00:09:47.382
Skip it when nobody will update the map.

